<div id="S4.SS6.SSSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Key trends: (1) semantic representation learning improves over static baselines; (2) retrieval helps but is insufficient; (3) VulnAgent-X gains widen on realistic benchmarks (contextual reasoning/false-positive control).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS6.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Commit-level detection and localisation</h4>

<div id="S4.SS6.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Commit-level detection and localisation ‣ 4.6 Main results ‣ 4 Experimental Design and Results ‣ VulnAgent-X: A Layered Agentic Framework for Repository-Level Vulnerability Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows VulnAgent-X achieves strongest commit-level F1 and localisation performance (Top-1/Top-3 accuracy, MRR), with moderate runtime overhead acceptable for security-critical code review.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Just-in-time vulnerability detection and localisation results.</figcaption>
